---
import Icon from "../Icon.astro";
---

<section class="section container local-storage-grid">
  <div class="local-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow section-label">03 / NO CLOUD HANGING OVER YOU</p>
    <h2>
      Your saves stay
      <br />
      on your machine.
    </h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      Your save history belongs to you. Save Scum works locally and stores
      snapshots on storage you control.
    </p>
    <ul class="privacy-list">
      {[
        "No account",
        "No subscription",
        "No cloud required",
        "No telemetry",
        "Portable archives",
        "Works offline",
      ].map((label) => (
        <li>
          <Icon name="check" size={16} />
          {label}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="small-copy">
      Local history protects against a bad save. An extra copy on another device
      protects against a bad drive.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="storage-panel">
    <div class="storage-title">
      <Icon name="folder" size={23} />
      <span class="micro-label">LESS COPYING. MORE KEEPING.</span>
    </div>
    <h3>
      Hundreds of snapshots.
      <br />
      Not hundreds of copies.
    </h3>
    <p>
      Unchanged files are shared between snapshots. New file contents are
      hashed, compressed, and stored once.
    </p>
    <div
      class="dedup-diagram"
      aria-label="Snapshots 41, 42, and 43 share the same world save. Changed player saves use separate stored files."
    >
      <div>
        <span>snapshot 41</span>
        <span>snapshot 42</span>
        <span>snapshot 43</span>
      </div>
      <div class="dedup-lines" aria-hidden="true">
        ⎫<br />⎬<br />⎭
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="blob">
          world.sav <b>one shared file</b>
        </span>
        <small>player.sav changes → new file</small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-copy">
      Illustrative file relationships. Storage savings depend on your saves;
      compression does not guarantee a particular ratio.
    </p>
    <a href="/features/#storage" class="text-link">
      Inside snapshot storage <Icon size={15} />
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
